{"id":"word:hebrew:H3282","type":"word","title":"יַעַן","subtitle":"H3282 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, heed ; by implication, purpose (sake or account); used adverbially to indicate the reason or cause","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יַעַן (H3282) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: conj.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 99 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יַעַן (yaʻan) means properly, heed ; by implication, purpose (sake or account); used adverbially to indicate the reason or cause First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 3 11."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יַעַן","transliteration":"yaʻan","pronunciation":"yah'-an","strong":"H3282","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3282","partOfSpeech":"conj","forms":["יַ֚עַן","יַ֗עַן","יַ֣עַן","יַ֛עַן","יַ֤עַן"],"morphs":[["HC",96],["HC/R/C",2],["HR/C",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, heed ; by implication, purpose (sake or account); used adverbially to indicate the reason or cause","usage":"because (that), forasmuch ( as), seeing then, that, whereas, why.","full":"H3282. yaan I. יַ֫עַן preposition and conjunction see below I. ענה . יַעַן 96 properly substantive , purpose, intention , but always used as preposition or conjunction , on account of, because (for יַעֲנֶה , of the form יִצְהָר etc., Sta § 259 Kö ii. 403 ; compare mean, intend ): — 1 as preposition , rarely with a substantive, Ezek 5:9 תּוֺעֲבוֺתֵיכֶם יַעַן , Hag 1:9 מָה יַעַן , 1:9 בֵּיתִי יַעַן ; with a participle Ezek 36:13 אמרים יען because of men saying to you (but read probably אָמְרָם , Co Toy Berthol); frequently with infinitive with, 1Kin 21:20 הִתְמַכֶּרְךָ יַעַן on account of thy having sold thyself, Amos 5:11 ; Isa 30:12 ; 37:29 (= 2Kin 19:28 ) אֵלַי הִתְרַגֶּזְךָ יַעֵן , Jer 5:14 ; 7:13 ; 23:38 ; 48:7 , and often. (c. 18 t.) in Ezek., as 5:7 (read הַמְרֹתְכֶם יַעַן ), 13:8 , 22 ; 25:3 , 6 , 8 , 12 . 2 As conjunction : a. אֲשֶׁר יַעַן (32 t.), usually with perfect, as Gen 22:16 זאת עשׂית אשׁר יען because that thou hast done this, Deut 1:36 ( Josh 14:14 ), Judg 2:20 ; 1Sam 30:22 ; 1Kin 3:11 ; 8:18 ; Jer 19:4 ; 25:8 ; 29:23 (not Isaiah) +; with imperfect (in frequent. sense) Ezek 44:12 . b. כִּי יַען , Num 11:20 אֶתיֿ מְאַסְתֶּם כִּי ׳יַעַן , 1Kin 13:21 ; 21:29 ; Isa 3:16 ; 7:5 ; 8:6 ; 29:13 . c. יַעַן alone (23 t.), with perfect Num 20:12 בִּי הֶאֱמַנְתֶּם לֹא יַעַן , 1Sam 15:23 ; 1Kin 14:13 ; 20:42 ; 2Kin 22:19 ; Hosea 8:1 ; Isa 61:1 ; 65:12 ; 66:4 ; with imperfect (frequently) Ezek 34:21 ; of the future 12:12 because he shall not see, etc., (but ᵐ5 Co Kau Berthol לָעַיִן יֵרָאֶה לא אשׁר לְמַעַן ): usually the verb follows immediately, but Ezek. sometimes puts the object first for emphasis, 5:11 טִמֵּאתָ אֶתמִֿקְדָּשִׁי יַעַן , 20:16 , 24 ; 36:6 , compare 34:21 . 3 וּבְיַעַן יַעַן , q.d. because and by the cause (that), followed by perhaps, Lev 26:43 (H) מָאָ֔סוּ בְּמִשְׁמָּטַי וביען יען , Ezek 13:10 ; בְּיַעַז יַעַן followed by infinitive, 36:3 . (In all, reckoning (ו)ביען יען once each, 93 t., of which 20 are in 1-2 Kings, 11 in Jeremiah, 38 in Ezekiel; and only 9 in Genesis&#8212;2Samuel.)","rootNote":"from an unused root meaning to pay attention;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 3 11","keyReferences":["1Kgs 3 11","1Kgs 8 18","1Kgs 11 11","1Kgs 11 33","1Kgs 13 21","1Kgs 14 7","1Kgs 14 13","1Kgs 14 15"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":99,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Kgs 3 11","book":"1Kgs","chapter":3,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַעַן֩","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC"},{"reference":"1Kgs 8 18","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַ֗עַן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 11","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יַ֚עַן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 33","book":"1